{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"c999dd8447b9295ddf080c3751c119d56e7dc20bd2af7e83f21deaf10fffd604","digest":{"component_or_area":"metrics packaging and optional dependencies","key_entities":["src/rebar/_optional.EXTRAS","src/rebar/metrics/analyzer.py","guard_import","OptionalDependencyError","lizard","project.optional-dependencies","pyproject.toml","import-linter"],"problem_keywords":["optional dependency","lazy import","metrics extra","guard import","lizard","optional-dependencies","dependency-free core"],"propositions":["The metrics module and its lizard dependency must be packaged as an optional [metrics] extra, with metrics registered in _optional.EXTRAS and referenced in guard_import.","Core-only installations must import rebar and rebar.metrics cleanly without lizard, with guard_import raising OptionalDependencyError that adapters catch and convert to Unavailable.","The analyzer.py must lazily import lizard only when guard_import succeeds, never at package import time, to maintain the dependency-free import path for core.","External CLI tools scc and jscpd must be detected at runtime and are not pip dependencies.","A test must verify that missing the metrics extra triggers Unavailable and that import-linter optionality checks pass."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787690914884713001,"uuid":"64389051-ae7d-49b1-8716-726069b030b8"}